Subject: a member's log on a simulated device, its cuts and work in flight, a planted defect, the owed redirects in order
Why: Quiver's persisted class runs in a deterministic simulation (kiln's CP-T2.2 step 6, docs/design/persisted-sim.md). A member opens its log on hyper-sim's block device under hyper-log's Waits::Told (NodeFile, Member::open_simulated; the sim feature). Its host cuts and serves it (Member::cut, serve) at the virtual time the node's disk draws, and reads its work in flight (Member::in_flight). Member::plant reaches the planted defect (the mutants feature). The acknowledgements a member owed are redirected in order when it stops leading, not in a HashMap's. Offered to Focal.

